{"step_index":141,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-28T19:02:51Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-28T15:02:51-04:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-28T15:02:51-04:00\nFile Path: `file:///Volumes/Untitled/SSOT_Agentic_Brain_v1.1.0_ENGINEERING_RELEASE/ops/scripts/agent_speak.sh`\nTotal Lines: 56\nTotal Bytes: 1682\nShowing lines 1 to 56\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: #!/usr/bin/env bash\n2: # =============================================================================\n3: # XORAS SYSTEM: AGENT SPEAK DISPATCHER (USB WORKSPACE)\n4: # Tries ElevenLabs first (if API key set), otherwise falls back to macOS `say`.\n5: # Uses Cocoa voice \"Onyx\" when available; otherwise defaults to Daniel.\n6: # =============================================================================\n7: set -eu\n8: \n9: AGENT=\"${1:-maxx}\"\n10: RAW_TEXT=\"${2:-}\"\n11: \n12: # Validate input\n13: if [[ -z \"${RAW_TEXT//[[:space:]]/}\" ]]; then\n14:   echo \"[agent_speak] refused empty speech payload\" >&2\n15:   exit 2\n16: fi\n17: \n18: # Helper: invoke ElevenLabs via the provided JS helper if the key exists.\n19: use_elevenlabs() {\n20:   local text=\"$1\"\n21:   # Path to the ElevenLabs helper script (relative to this script)\n22:   local script=\"/Volumes/Untitled/SSOT_Agentic_Brain_v1.1.0_ENGINEERING_RELEASE/AI_Core/Xoras_Project/xoras-core/Source/elevenlabs_say.mjs\"\n23:   if [[ -f \"$script\" ]]; then\n24:     node \"$script\" \"$text\"\n25:     return $?\n26:   else\n27:     return 1\n28:   fi\n29: }\n30: \n31: # Determine which voice to use for native macOS `say`\n32: native_voice=\"Daniel\"\n33: # Prefer Onyx if installed (check via `say -v \"Onyx\"` exit code)\n34: if say -v \"Onyx\" \"\" 2>/dev/null; then\n35:   native_voice=\"Onyx\"\n36: fi\n37: